WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.538
A blank string is not NULL in PostgreSQL An empty
string is

00:00:04.562 --> 00:00:08.175
a known text value with zero characters and a
whitespace-only string is

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:12.262
also a real value until spaces are removed This
matters when a

00:00:12.288 --> 00:00:16.988
rule says no usable email Testing only IS NULL would
miss empty

00:00:17.012 --> 00:00:22.888
text and whitespace-only text BTRIM removes
surrounding spaces NULLIF

00:00:22.912 --> 00:00:28.038
then converts an empty trimmed result to NULL After
that normalization IS

00:00:28.062 --> 00:00:32.775
NULL can treat the three cases consistently Run the
example and inspect

00:00:32.788 --> 00:00:37.900
the patients returned This is a practical
preparation pattern because messy text

00:00:37.925 --> 00:00:40.925
often needs normalization before business rules are
applied
